Value Lab

Value lab today 3 PM and this is the code

You are given a list of transactions. Each transaction contains:
Transaction ID
Customer ID
Amount
Status
Write Java code to:
Filter only transactions with SUCCESS status.
Group successful transactions by customer ID.
Calculate the total transaction amount for each customer.
Print the customer ID and total successful transaction amount.

Sample input
class Transaction {
   private int transactionId;
   private int customerId;
   private double amount;
   private String status;

   // Constructor and getters
}

List<Transaction> transactions = Arrays.asList(
   new Transaction(101, 1, 500, "SUCCESS"),
   new Transaction(102, 2, 700, "FAILED"),
   new Transaction(103, 1, 300, "SUCCESS"),
   new Transaction(104, 2, 200, "SUCCESS"),
   new Transaction(105, 3, 400, "SUCCESS"),
   new Transaction(106, 1, 100, "FAILED")
);

Expected output
Customer ID: 1, Total: 800
Customer ID: 2, Total: 200
Customer ID: 3, Total: 400

Filter only transactions with SUCCESS status.

transactions.stream().filter(t-> t.getStatus().equals("STATUS")).toList();
Group successful transactions by customer ID.
transactions.stream().collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Transaction::getCustomerId, Colletions.filteringBy(t->t.getStatus().equals("SUCCESS"), Collectors.toList())));
transactions.stream().filter(t->t.getStatus().equals("SUCCESS")).collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Transaction::getCustomerId, Collectors.toList()));

Calculate the total transaction amount for each customer.
transactions.stream().collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Transaction::getCustomerId, Collectors.summingDouble(Transaction::getAmount())));

Print the customer ID and total successful transaction amount.

transactions.stream().filter(t->t.getStatus().equals("SUCCESS")).collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Transaction::getCustomerId, Collectors.summingDouble(Transaction::getAmount())))
.entrySet().stream().forEach(map-> System.out.println(map.getKey()+" : "+ map.getValue()));